{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting","id":153601,"title":"Help with setting up a Philadelphia setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-30T01:13:12-07:00","id":153601,"title":"Help with setting up a Philadelphia setting","content":"So yeah I'm planning to run a game that may be set in the city of Philadelphia and could use some help. I've been to the city so I know of several important locations and history what I need help with is who are the major players in the city. The game line doesn't matter any info given would be helpful also what books if any would help me with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:13:52-07:00","id":153713,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Prince is or was William Penn? He certainly has the personality of an anarch Ventrue coming to the new world to form his own domain away from the elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:33:32-07:00","id":154099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin404</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting#post153601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah I'm planning to run a game that may be set in the city of Philadelphia and could use some help. I've been to the city so I know of several important locations and history what I need help with is who are the major players in the city. The game line doesn't matter any info given would be helpful also what books if any would help me with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter the Vigil corebook is set in the city of Philadelphia. Some good info in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:13:03-07:00","id":154174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin404</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting#post153601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah I'm planning to run a game that may be set in the city of Philadelphia and could use some help. I've been to the city so I know of several important locations and history what I need help with is who are the major players in the city. The game line doesn't matter any info given would be helpful also what books if any would help me with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you can use for plothooks or what supernatural stuff is going on:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.weirdus.com/states/pennsylvania/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Weird US: Pennsylvania section of the site </a><br /> The book usually has more than just the website does, so here's the links for it on <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Weird-Pennsylvania-Pennsylvanias-Legends-Secrets/dp/1402766866\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon</a> or <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/weird-pennsylvania-mark-moran/1100000932?ean=9781402766862\" target=\"_blank\">B&amp;N</a>.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Philadelphia-Haunts-Eastern-Penitentiary-Mifflin/dp/0764329871/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1401483927&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=Philadelphia+supernatural\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Philadelphia Haunts: At Eastern State Penitentiary, Fort Mifflin, and Other Ghostly Sites</span></a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Forgotten-Tales-Philadelphia-Thomas-White/dp/1609492706/ref=sr_1_28?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1401484030&amp;sr=8-28&amp;keywords=Philadelphia+supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">Forgotten Tales of Philadelphia</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 05-30-2014, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T16:50:05-07:00","id":154297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting?p=154099#post154099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter the Vigil corebook is set in the city of Philadelphia. Some good info in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this is going to be a cWOD game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T17:44:32-07:00","id":154385,"title":"","content":"Well, I started looking through my old W:tA databases, here's what I could find (<i>Which wasn't much</i>):<br /> <br /> <b>Caerns:</b> (<b>Name</b>/<b>Level/Gauntlet/Type/Tribe Structure/Totem/Location/Pg. #/Book Title</b>)<br /> Woodheart Caern ? ? ? Fianna ? Pennsylvania 95 Apocalypse<br /> Mountain Laurel Caern ? ? ? Multitribal? ? Pennsylvania 102 Drums Around the Fire<br /> <br /> <b>Characters:</b><br /> Randy Internet (Glass Walker) Philadelphia 151 Wyrm Wolf<br /> Leonard Gateway (Glass Walker) Philadelphia 152 Wyrm Wolf<br /> Roland Gateway (Glass Walker) Philadelphia 152 Wyrm Wolf<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>Fera that would/might be in this area:</b></u><br /> Ananasi<br /> Corax<br /> Gurahl<br /> Nuwisha<br /> Pumonca<br /> Qualmi<br /> Ratkin<br /> <br /> <u><b>Garou Tribes:</b></u> (Philadelphia is probably heavily dominated/in control by either the Get of Fenris or Glass Walkers.)<br /> Black Furies<br /> Bone Gnawers<br /> Children of Gaia<br /> Fianna<br /> Get of Fenris<br /> Glass Walkers<br /> Red Talons (<i>Very rare</i>)<br /> Shadow Lords<br /> Silent Striders (<i>As they come and go</i>)<br /> Silver Fangs<br /> Stargazers (<i>If any are still around</i>)<br /> Uktena<br /> Wendigo<br /> (<i>Not to mention a ton of Black Spiral Dancers</i>)<br /> <br /> Philadelphia also probably has a City Father Spirit associated with it that takes on the appearance of Benjamin Franklin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:05:24-07:00","id":154402,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Vigil: Night Stalkers also has a fair amount of info on Philadelphia's local Kindred. To sum it up, there's no Prince and a three-way struggle for power between the Carthians, Ordo Dracul and Invictus. (The lack of Prince was probably because the NWoD's Philadelphia was designed with a Hunter game in mind--no overarching Kindred authority makes it easier for hunter PCs to get away with staking vamps, allying with one faction to take down another, and causing other trouble).<br /> <br /> If I were to convert what was there to the CWoD, I'd have the Carthians be mostly Brujah Anarchs, recast the Invictus as Ventrue, and turn the Ordo Dracul into Tremere. Depending on how high a power level you want in your Philadelphia, I could see a Tremere Lord or Pontifex making their haven in the city (what with its long history, universities and economic importance). The Toreador would also be attracted to the city's art.<br /> <br /> I'd throw in the Sabbat as another faction, given Philly's history of violence. Their influence has probably declined in recent years as the city's gotten better, but of course they wouldn't be all gone (where's the fun in that?). Nearby Camden still suffers from some of the worst crime rates and political corruption in the US, so the Sabbat and Follwers of Set could both have a strong presence there. The population isn't big enough to support many Kindred (77k), but since it's only 5 miles away from Philly, the resident Kindred could poach from Camarilla domains every night and then flee back to Camden. An absent Prince would forestall any strong response. (And if you prefer to hand-wave Kindred population logistics, the Sabbat/Setites engaging in nightly mass poaching still sets up a lot of potential conflicts.) Actually, the Setites would probably try to come to a peaceful arrangement that gets themselves blood. Setting themselves up as open enemies isn't their style.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Giovanni could have a strong presence too. Philly's a center of finance, its Mafia is one of the most active in the US, and as an old (and violent) city it'll have a lot of ghosts. Perfect for their needs.<br /> <br /> Regarding more specific figures, Critias (the Brujah Primogen from Chicago by Night) is supposed to have been Prince in at least several American cities. He fell in love with American democracy after encountering it, so it's a natural fit to have him rule as Prince over its birthplace. To keep this relevant to modern-night Philly, perhaps Critias sired a childe while there or brought along an older one from Europe who decided to hang around after his sire left. Said childe could be the Curator, an uber-powerful Kindred scholar and &quot;boss monster&quot; for hunters mentioned in Night Stalkers. (In fact, I think that shakes things up nicely to have a Brujah be the most prominent scholar in a city rather than a Tremere. The old school Brujah don't get much rep.) A 6th-generation Kindred could well fill that role, particularly if he was Embraced centuries earlier and followed his sire to the New World. This version of the Curator probably would've had a falling out with Critias after coming to Philly, as it doesn't make much sense for him to cross the Atlantic with his sire and then decide Chicago is too far a move. Enemies of the Curator might well be able to find aid in the Windy City.<br /> <br /> I think Counsel of Primogen also had some passing info on Philadelphia in the CWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T21:52:03-07:00","id":154514,"title":"","content":"Thank You guys for helping with what Kindred and Garou would be in filly, what about Mages would any of them, be in Philly? Or Changelings specially the ones nWOD. No need for you guys to give me help on the Wraith aspects, Pen. State gives me enough material to work with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T05:03:49-07:00","id":154705,"title":"","content":"The Jersey Devil would be good for a fae outside the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T09:27:10-07:00","id":154920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin404</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting?p=154297#post154297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except this is going to be a cWOD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that since, you know, this was posted in the CWOD section of the forums.<br /> <br /> Hunter the Vigil's version of Philadelphia still has the basic infrastructure and info needed to base a game around it, whether CWOD or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T10:56:11-07:00","id":155002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/153601-help-with-setting-up-a-philadelphia-setting?p=154705#post154705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jersey Devil would be good for a fae outside the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one is a bit iffy, as it can also qualify as a Chimera and many other things as well (<i>Like a Wyld Gorgon</i>). I think the Jersey Devil does appear in Hunter: the Reckoning's Urban Legends book and has something to do with vampires.<br /> <br /> Pennsylvania has a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairie_Festival\" target=\"_blank\">Fairie Festival</a>. And with the <a href=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/page.php?109.4\" target=\"_blank\">map</a> from C:tD, Pennsylvania is under the Kingdom of Apples. Most of what was written about the Kingdom of Apples focused on New York, New Jersey, Boston, or Connecticut (<i>Freeholds &amp; Glens</i>).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forsaken-kingdom.blogspot.com/2011/07/map-kingdom-of-apples.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Long Forsaken Kingdom link</a>. I don't know anything about Changeling: the Lost, if you are wanting to use that instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 05-31-2014, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}